BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TO EXPLAIN THE WORLD: Revisiting Restrepo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260420T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260420T210000
UID:blogto-233663@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/14/original_image640dee42-49fb-45e0-b962-4f866b1e8c
 72.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Restrepo (2010)\, co-directed by Sebastian Junger and Tim Heth
 erington\, follows a platoon of U.S. soldiers deployed in Afghanistan’s 
 Korengal Valley. Shot over the course of a year\, the film offers an intim
 ate\, unfiltered look at life on the front lines.\nThis screening marks 15
  years since the death of photojournalist and filmmaker Tim Hetherington. 
 The evening will include a brief excerpt from a recorded conversation with
  Tim Hetherington from 2009\, and a recent conversation with Sebastian Jun
 ger\, followed by an open discussion on witnessing\, authorship\, and what
  it means to “be there” in an era of AI and mediated images.
LOCATION:Innis College Deluxe Screening Room and Lounge
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/to-explain-the-world-revisiting-restrepo
 -toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
