DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260425T185200
UID:blogto-233195@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/06/original_image11530fcc-d484-4b92-bde3-3229e2134b
 b9.jpg
DESCRIPTION:From April 23 to May 3\, the 2026 Hot Docs Festival will prese
 nt documentaries from around the world to audiences in Toronto. 115 films 
 from 51 countries will screen during this year's Festival. Tickets are on 
 sale now.\nSince her first appearance in L. Frank Baum’s The Wonderful W
 izard of Oz in 1900\, Dorothy Gale has enchanted generations with her cour
 age\, curiosity and determined search for home. What is it about her story
  that still feels so relatable\, especially to those whose experiences are
 n’t always centred? It’s Dorothy! invites audiences on a dazzling jour
 ney through Dorothy’s enduring cultural legacy\, tracing her profound im
 pact on women\, folks of colour\, and LGBTQ+ communities. The film weaves 
 a poignant portrait of Judy Garland’s life and her connection to those w
 ho see themselves in Dorothy\, blending mesmerizing archival footage from 
 Garland’s career and the classic 1939 musical film The Wizard of Oz with
  insights from contemporary voices including Ashanti\, Margaret Cho\, Lena
  Waithe and John Waters. At once fantastical and deeply human\, It’s Dor
 othy! reminds us that through self-love\, the celebration of imagination\,
  and the radical power of belonging\, there truly is no place like home. S
 imone Estrin
LOCATION:TIFF Lightbox
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/its-dorothy-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:It's in the Cards
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260425T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260425T220000
UID:blogto-232643@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/24/original_image77331faa-db3c-4725-bea2-6cb95722e2
 86.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Bars look social from the outside\, but most people just stick
  to the group they came with. It’s surprisingly hard to meet anyone new 
 in public spaces.\nAt It’s in the Cards\, talking to other people is the
  whole point. You get a card when you arrive and trade it throughout the n
 ight to try and get the one you want. It’s all in good fun and designed 
 to create conversation\, so talking to people you don’t know is not only
  allowed\, it’s expected and easy.\nAt the end of the night\, we do a dr
 aw where 1 in 3 people win a real gift card to the place they’re holding
 \, so make sure it’s somewhere you like.\nDesigned for those aged 30 and
  up. Everyone 19+ is welcome.\nApril 25\, 7:00 PM to 10:00 PM\nLiberty Vil
 lage (private event space)\nTickets: $35 early bird (includes a drink)\, $
 45 regular
LOCATION:Private event space in Liberty Village
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/its-in-the-cards-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
