BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:American Doctor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260428T051500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260428T191800
UID:blogto-233190@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/06/original_image5ce087b2-4ae5-4a76-9110-bbcebbe203
 11.jpg
DESCRIPTION:From April 23 to May 3\, the 2026 Hot Docs Festival will prese
 nt documentaries from around the world to audiences in Toronto. 115 films 
 from 51 countries will screen during this year's Festival. Tickets are on 
 sale now.\nThree US doctors on the ground in Gaza risk everything to save 
 lives and expose the horrors they encounter. Despite their differing backg
 rounds—Palestinian\, Jewish and Zoroastrian—the physicians are steadfa
 st in providing emergency medical care amid a growing humanitarian crisis 
 while at the same time demanding action and accountability from their gove
 rnment. Director Poh Si Teng doesn’t censor what she witnesses in Gaza l
 est she engage in what one of the doctors calls “journalistic malpractic
 e.” Filmed in several hospitals under siege\, the documentary captures t
 he unfolding chaos of emergency medicine in a devastated healthcare system
 \, where physicians must make unfathomable triage decisions while confront
 ing danger themselves. Moving between frontline medical care and the corri
 dors of government power\, American Doctor explores the moral responsibili
 ties of healthcare workers in times of conflict and the fragile intersecti
 on of medicine\, politics and humanitarian action. Vivian Belik\n \nConte
 nt advisory: This film contains scenes of graphic medical imagery.
LOCATION:TIFF Lightbox
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/american-doctor-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
