BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Conservation and Curation - Iron Gall Ink
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260428T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260428T200000
UID:blogto-231923@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/09/original_image15615687-9039-4928-ac0d-36981a8f55
 13.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Did you ever wonder what goes on behind the scenes when we dev
 elop exhibitions? We’re peeking behind the curtain of Loops\, Swoops and
  Curlicues with the exhibition’s lead conservator\, Wendy McPhee\, to le
 arn about iron gall ink\, one of the most prevalent inks used in manuscrip
 ts (handwritten works).\nWendy will tell you about the components of the i
 nk and how it was made as well as the perils of iron gall ink. She will re
 veal the role of conservation in the curatorial process and show you some 
 before and after shots of the treatment of some of the items in the exhibi
 t. We'll have nibbed pens and sample pages from a penmanship instructional
  book from 1881 as well to finish off the talk!\nA corresponding short inf
 ormal chat in the TD Gallery will be available after the end of the formal
  program with our conservator.\nThis program is free to the public\; howev
 er\, we please ask that you register to secure your spot.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library - Beeton Hall
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/conservation-and-curation-iron-gall-ink-
 toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
