BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Open Studio
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T203000
UID:blogto-233061@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/02/original_imagefe9d3e2d-8050-4d49-b727-ea2b0311d0
 26.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Open Studio\, a space to explore your creativity\,
  connect with others\, and simply create without judgment. Whether you wan
 t to doodle\, colour\, write\, or just relax\, this is your time to do wha
 t inspires you\, alongside like-minded folks.\n​​​Open Studio is mor
 e than a creative outlet. It’s a place to find rest\, connection\, and a
  little relief from daily pressures—a communal experience rooted in care
  and play.\n​​​A portion of proceeds from each will be donated to th
 e Parkdale Food Bank\, supporting nourishment and community care in our ne
 ighbourhood.\n​​​Let’s create together.\n​​​About Re-Work\n
 ​Re-Work is a Community First\n​We're a professional (and personal) de
 velopment community helping people redefine work\, ambition\, and success 
 on their own terms. We want you to get to a healthier\, less stress-filled
  place with the thing we spend most of our lives doing: working. Move beyo
 nd burnout toward work that is meaningful and fulfilling as your fullest s
 elf. Through a proven process and framework\, we help you craft a more sus
 tainable and values-aligned relationship with work. Through workshops\, st
 orytelling\, and community spaces\, Re-Work invites you to explore a healt
 hier\, more sustainable way of working and living.\n​\nLet’s build a f
 uture of work that works for you.
LOCATION:Issues Magazine Shop
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/open-studio-toronto-3/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
