BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:When a Witness Recants
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T201200
UID:blogto-233207@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/06/original_image9940d353-179c-4023-90b6-671bc5dd04
 86.jpg
DESCRIPTION:From April 23 to May 3\, the 2026 Hot Docs Festival will prese
 nt documentaries from around the world to audiences in Toronto. 115 films 
 from 51 countries will screen during this year's Festival. Tickets are on 
 sale now.\nAuthor Ta-Nehisi Coates reflects on and revisits the case of th
 e murder of a young boy inside the walls of a Baltimore middle school. Dec
 ades ago\, three teenagers were convicted of the crime\, then incarcerated
  for 36 years. Upon a deeper look into the incident\, layers start to peel
  away\, bringing to light how facts were severely skewed—and the truth t
 hat these men were convicted of a crime they did not commit. Through coerc
 ed false testimonies\, lives were changed forever. The profound impact of 
 that sentencing still shows how unjustly the Black community is treated al
 l too often by the US justice system. Hot Docs alum Dawn Porter (Luther: N
 ever Too Much\, opening night 2024) brings forth a powerful and stirring n
 ew film that looks at the trauma cases like this cause\, and the fight for
  retribution that still goes on today. Gabor Pertic
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/when-a-witness-recants-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
