BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CANADIAN PREMIERE of 'CEREMONY' at Hot Docs Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T193000
UID:blogto-233658@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/14/original_imagef1a304f8-31db-4e97-b02e-85e2fca0c7
 be.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Watch the Canadian Premiere of Banchi Hanuse's powerful docume
 ntary 'CEREMONY' at the Hot Docs Film Festival on Thursday\, April 30 at 5
 :30pm (TIFF Lightbox 1\, 350 King Street W) followed by a panel discussion
  with the director and special guests.  There will be an additional screen
 ing on Friday\, May 1 at 11:30am (TIFF Lightbox 2).\nWatch the Canadian Pr
 emiere of Banchi Hanuse's powerful documentary 'CEREMONY' at the Hot Docs 
 Film Festival on Thursday\, April 30 at 5:30pm (TIFF Lightbox 1\, 350 King
  Street W) followed by a panel discussion with the director and special gu
 ests.  There will be an additional screening on Friday\, May 1 at 11:30am 
 (TIFF Lightbox 2).\nAbout the Film:\nWhen the ooligan vanishes from Bella 
 Coola\, its absence remains like a scar\, pointing to a history that reach
 es far beyond the river. From a remote radio station on the edge of the wo
 rld\, Nuxalk voices rise through crackling airwaves to trace a truth no on
 e was meant to uncover. What begins as a local broadcast becomes an awaken
 ing\, confronting the systems built to erase them. Testimony\, watercolour
  animation and rare archival weave a story of survival\, return and the qu
 iet revolution of an Indigenous Nation that refuses to disappear.\nThis is
 n't just a premiere. It's CEREMONY.\nWatch the trailer and buy tickets @ h
 ttps://hotdocs.ca
LOCATION:TIFF Lightbox
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/canadian-premiere-of-ceremony-at-hot-doc
 s-festival-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ceramic Workshop: Build a Candle Holder or Incense Holder
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T210000
UID:blogto-233342@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/08/original_image695b9e62-78bf-45f3-b8fd-78923b25c9
 a7.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Explore hand-building techniques to create one-of-a-kind candl
 e holders or incense burners out of clay with guidance from Emily Elise!\n
 In this 2.5 hour workshop\, we will build a custom incense holder or candl
 e holder using stoneware clay. This class is open to all levels of experie
 nce\, including beginners!\nThe bulk of the workshop will be focused on ha
 nd-building forms\, using slab-rolling techniques and shape language to bu
 ild up our clay into a functional object. A demo will be provided at the b
 eginning of the workshop and guidance will be provided throughout.\nWith o
 ur remaining time we will have the option to glaze/paint custom designs on
  our greenware (semi-hardened clay).\nEach piece will then be taken to a c
 eramic studio to be bisque fired\, and dipped in a clear top coat of glaze
  and then fired once more.\nFinal works will be available for pickup at Lo
 ohoo within 3-4 weeks.\nAbout the facilitator:\nEmily Elise is a visual ar
 tist and ceramicist working out of Kitte Club in the Junction and her home
  studio in Grange Park. Emily has a background in illustration and began h
 er ceramics journey in 2025 and loves to share what she's learned along th
 e way! Check our her portfolio!\nAbout Loohoo:\nLoohoo is a cute concept g
 ift shop in Parkdale\, designed to feel like a dreamy apartment — playfu
 l\, colourful\, and weird. Think: cute stuff for your cute life\, thoughtf
 ully curated with whimsy and a touch of unhinged energy.\nLoohoo is also a
  creative community space\, hosting themed markets\, workshops\, intimate 
 concerts\, and any fun ideas we can dream up to bring the community togeth
 er to play and celebrate local creators.\n💕 Follow along on Instagram @
 shop.loohoo to see what’s new in the shop!
LOCATION:Loohoo
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/ceramic-workshop-build-a-candle-holder-o
 r-incense-holder-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Designing the Movies: His Girl Friday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T184500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T210000
UID:blogto-231014@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/02/17/original_image7fedef71-7fe3-4b7b-b2b2-0b133a1339
 ea.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The fast and furiously funny screwball comedy classic! Suave n
 ewspaper editor Walter Burns (Cary Grant) learns his former star reporter 
 and ex-wife Hildy Johnson (Rosalind Russell) is engaged to a boring insura
 nce man (Ralph Bellamy)—naturally\, he plots sabotage. Can Hildy triumph
  in a battle of wills against her old romantic sparring partner and\, more
  importantly\, can she resist the possibility of a scoop? Howard Hawks dir
 ects Charles Lederer’s breathless screenplay with frenzied abandon. Verb
 al wit\, slapstick\, social satire\, farce and absurdity combine with roma
 ntic comedy\, gender politics\, and commentary on corruption in the justic
 e system. From press room card games to jailhouse interviews\, the fast-ta
 lking hijinks are an early example of the overlapping dialogue that influe
 nced Altman\, Sorkin and many others. 4K restoration\, presented with an i
 ntroduction by series host Nathalie Atkinson. $18/$15
LOCATION:Revue Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/designing-the-movies-his-girl-friday-tor
 onto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ELECTRIC BLUE NOTE Concert -- an INTERNATIONAL JAZZ DAY event!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T230000
UID:blogto-233636@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/14/original_image031634f3-7fc2-462c-b2c1-ea7aa969f0
 d8.jpg
DESCRIPTION:ELECTRIC BLUE NOTE Concert\n(electric-jazz versions of Blue No
 te classics)\n-- an INTERNATIONAL JAZZ DAY event! --\n----\nCelebrate Inte
 rnational Jazz Day in Toronto with a night of legendary selections from th
 e iconic Blue Note Records jazz label\, featuring jazz iconoclast BROWNMAN
  ALI and an all-star cast of Toronto’s top-tier players\, re-imagining t
 hese innovative Blue Note arrangements through the lens of electric-jazz\,
  as Miles Davis might have done. Known internationally for his work with t
 he BROWNMAN ELECTRYC TRIO\, a GRAMMY Award long-lister & 2x National Jazz 
 Award winner for Electric Jazz Group of the Year\, Brownman has been haile
 d by NPR in New York City as “the new standard in electric-jazz.” Audi
 ences can expect deep-groove interpretations of Blue Note classics\, where
  the rhythmic language of modern Black American Music collides with the ha
 rmonic daring of the label’s golden era. “We love taking classic jazz 
 repertoire and re-imagining them through the electric-jazz lens"\, states 
 Brownman\, "as if it were written today and produced by someone like DJ Pr
 emier or Flying Lotus. The goal is to create something that sounds complet
 ely current\, but still resonates with the history and lineage of the Blue
  Note jazz tradition.” And yes\, you’ll definitely hear plenty of Mile
 s Davis’ influence -- Brownman's touchstone -- in the resulting electric
  Blue Note sound. Don't miss it!\n----\n:: BROWNMAN ALI - electric trumpet
 \n:: NICK MACLEAN - rhodes/synth\n:: SEAN DENNIS - 6-string electric bass\
 n:: AARON SEUNARINE - drums\n----\nThr-Apr-30 -- TORONTO\, ON @ My HOUSE\n
 2882 Dundas St. West\, Toronto\, ON\nwww.MyHouseInTheJunction.com\n6:00pm 
 - doors & dinner\n8:00pm - show\nTix: www.eventbrite.ca/e/1986687684344\n-
 ---\nNOTE: Club doors are open at 6pm. Perhaps consider coming early for d
 inner & enjoy the room ambiance\, the cocktail options & Brownman's Blue N
 ote DJ selections. Your concert ticket gets you in on a first come first s
 erve basis\, but please note those with dinner reservations are given seat
 ing preference. If you'd like to make a reservation\, please call (416) 60
 4 4555 or email info@myhouseinthejunction.com\nSee their award-winning men
 u:\nwww.myhouseinthejunction.com/menu\n----\nPresented by: My House & Brow
 ntasauras Records\n----\nABOUT BROWNMAN ALI | www.Brownman.com\nAn interna
 tionally acclaimed jazz iconoclast\, Brownman Ali is a 2x National Jazz Aw
 ard winner\; 10x Global Music Award winner\; 7x Toronto Independent Music 
 Award winner\; GRAMMY Award long-lister\; multiple JUNO Award nominee\; is
  heralded by the NY Village Voice as "Canada's preeminent jazz trumpet pla
 yer"\, and is best known as the last trumpet soloist for legendary jazz-hi
 p-hop outfit Guru's Jazzmatazz (replacing Donald Byrd in this iconic group
 ). Splitting his time between Toronto\, ON & Brooklyn\, NY\, when not lead
 ing 8 groups of his own (including the National Jazz Award winning BROWNMA
 N ELECTRYC TRIO & Montreal Jazz Fest's "Grand Prix du Jazz" winners CRUZAO
 )\, he is also a highly in-demand studio session musician having appeared 
 on over 300 recordings to date\, and is the CEO of the acclaimed Brooklyn-
 based record label BROWNTASAURAS RECORDS. His bombastically narrative styl
 e as an improviser\, often reminiscent of Miles Davis\, has made him one o
 f the most sought after soloists today.\n----\nCODA magazine writes:\n“.
 .. capturing the essence of the later years in Miles Davis’ life\, his e
 lectric period\, without imitation. Brownman's sound is uniquely his own..
 .. clearly paying apt tribute to Brownman’s NYC mentor Randy Brecker".\n
 ----\nBuffalo News writes:\n“Awards are nice\, naturally\, but to dig wh
 at Brownman is doing\, you’ve got to see him live. I had a chance to do 
 just that over the summer when Brownman fronted his killer trio ... I came
  away with a blown mind. This guy’s got chops galore\, soul to match\, a
 nd a sense of phrasing that recalls many of the greats\, but suggests itse
 lf to be his own.”\n----\nToronto’s NOW Magazine writes:\n“It’s in
 credible the energy output this trio can generate... my ears would swear t
 hey were hearing a whole big band at times”.
LOCATION:My House
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/electric-blue-note-concert-an-internatio
 nal-jazz-day-event-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
