BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lost Steps: Live Performance by Interspecies Musician David Rothen
 berg
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T210000
UID:blogto-233601@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/13/original_image67a04372-2caa-4123-8cd0-cce72bab84
 fd.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Stta: invites you to join us in collective listening\, as Davi
 d Rothenberg uses sound as a bridge between humans and other living beings
 .\nDavid Rothenberg is a distinguished listener\, musician\, philosopher\,
  and author\, engaging with the sounds around us\, not as background noise
 \, but as rich\, expressive “languages of life” waiting to be explored
 . Through collaboration with other species\, he emphasizes the connection 
 between humanity and the natural world. We invite you to join us in collec
 tive\, reflective listening.\n“We will not survive as artists or as a sp
 ecies if we cannot become part of the world that surrounds us. There shoul
 d be no duality between music and nature. Natural sound is never separable
  from human sound. The moment we decide to listen\, to seek out meaning\, 
 we start to change the world.”\n-David Rothenberg\, Sudden Music: Improv
 isation\, Sound\, Nature\, University of Georgia Press\, 2002.\nRothenberg
  approaches listening as an act of earthly survival. To engage deeply\, ex
 pressively\, and wonderfully with nature is to reconnect with a world from
  which we\, as a species\, have become increasingly disconnected.\nThis ev
 ent encourages deep listening and environmental awareness\, creative expre
 ssion through music and sound\, and a renewed sense of wonder about the na
 tural world.\n2 Performances:\nMay 2nd\, 2026 / 7:00 pm ET\nMay 3rd\, 2026
  / 2:00 pm ET (Children welcome to participate!)\nTickets will be availabl
 e April 21st.\nYou must have a ticket to gain entry. If you register\, but
  are unable to make it\, please show courtesy to the artist and attendees 
 by cancelling your ticket so someone can take your place.\nwww.somethingto
 thinkabout.nyc\nAs space is limited\, please do not bring any large bags o
 r backpacks. This is a shoes off event with seating on floor cushions or o
 n stools. Dress comfortably.
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/lost-steps-live-performance-by-interspec
 ies-musician-david-rothenberg-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
