 gto.com/events/2026/04/14/original_image93b4fdac-961f-416f-8bcb-2306c2a9cd
 76.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Make it a Mother’s Day outing at the movies with a musical d
 ouble feature that’s equal parts sparkle and heart. Start with Gold Digg
 ers of 1933\, the ultimate backstage crowd-pleaser\, featuring the famous 
 Busby Berkeley production numbers that basically invented “movie musical
  spectacle.” Then settle into Lili\, a tender\, charming story set aroun
 d a travelling carnival - a film that’s pure classic-Hollywood warmth. T
 his is the film that introduced the hit song Hi-Lili\, Hi-Lo! Two timeless
  films\, one great afternoon\, and a perfect excuse to go to the theatre!
LOCATION:Paradise Theatre
