 30.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A regular title on lists of the greatest Hollywood comedies\, 
 Some Like It Hot was released in 1959 and marked a peak in a hot streak fo
 r director Billy Wilder\, who also co-wrote the screenplay with regular co
 llaborator I.A.L. Diamond. The story of two down-and-out musicians fleeing
  from the mob by disguising themselves as women in an all-female band head
 ed to Florida offered plum roles for stars Marilyn Monroe\, Tony Curtis an
 d Jack Lemmon\, as well as memorable character roles for Joe E. Brown\, Ge
 orge Raft and Pat O'Brien. – The Academy\nMidtown Matinees revisits this
  enduring Hollywood classic in honour of Marilyn’s 100th birthday.
