BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Leven Kali
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T230000
UID:blogto-232443@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/20/original_imagedb150358-2568-48d5-86c4-4af1a5d3a6
 d1.jpg
DESCRIPTION:RAPSEASON and MRG Live present\nLeven Kali\nLK99 Tour\nLeven K
 ali (pronounced: Lay-Vin Kah-Li) is a Dutch-born\, L.A.-based singer\, son
 gwriter\, producer\, and multi-instrumentalist whose work fuses classic so
 ul musicianship with forward- thinking experimentation. He first broke thr
 ough with his Low Tide (2019) and HIGHTIDE (2020) mixtapes\, earning accla
 im for reintroducing emotional depth and live instrumentation to modern so
 ul.\nA sought-after collaborator\, Leven has written and produced for arti
 sts including Beyoncé\, Disclosure\, Teddy Swims\, and Playboi Carti\, re
 ceiving multiple GRAMMY® nominations for his work on Renaissance and COWB
 OY CARTER. In March\, Leven is set to release his highly anticipated new a
 lbum LK99\, following LK99: The Prelude and standout tracks like “Are U 
 Still\,” a project that expands his genre-fluid vision across funk\, R&B
 \, jazz\, and psychedelic soul while firmly positioning him as one of the 
 most innovative voices in contemporary music.
LOCATION:Adelaide HALL
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/leven-kali-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:4 Weeks to UNLEASH YOUR VOICE: A Women's Singing Program
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T213000
UID:blogto-231938@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/09/original_image85d6ebbc-f2f0-4466-b9f3-6c087623cb
 c2.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Sing\, grow\, and rise. Build joy and confidence in your authe
 ntic voice in a safe\, soulful circle of women. Beginners cherished.\nWhet
 her you’re new to singing\, love karaoke\, or simply miss the joy of usi
 ng your voice\, this warm and supportive circle is for you.\n.\nOver four 
 Wednesday evenings\, we sing together in a lovingly guided arc that allows
  trust\, confidence\, and connection to build week by week.\nFrom 6:30 - 9
 :30pm\, women are guided through a fun and engaging warm-up\, and an eveni
 ng of beautiful\, easy-to-learn mantras\, healing songs and high-vibe pop 
 tunes.\nWhat you’ll get:\n✅ 4 joyful\, song-filled evening intensives 
 (3 hours each) in person — from 6:30–9:30pm\n✅ Exclusive access to o
 ur private WhatsApp group to stay connected and inspired between sessions\
 n✅ A specially curated Spotify playlist so the joy\, confidence\, and mu
 sical expansion continue long after the workshop ends\nWhat You’ll Gain:
 \nLet go of perfectionism – Express freely without judgment\nExperience 
 joyful release – Through singing\, movement\, and safe group connection\
 nReclaim your natural confidence – In a soulful\, supportive circle of w
 omen\nCome for the singing\, leave more authentically YOU!\nAbout Your Gui
 de - Kira Callahan:\nKira (Founder\, Soul to Voice) is a singer and vocal 
 empowerment guide blending decades of music expertise with soulful profess
 ional coaching. She creates spaces where women shed limitations and discov
 er the joy\, power\, and freedom of their authentic voice. Her work is roo
 ted in deep respect\, safety\, and the belief that your voice matters.
LOCATION:The Smoking Frog
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/4-weeks-to-unleash-your-voice-a-womens-s
 inging-program-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
