BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cinema Shift Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T202000
UID:blogto-233704@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/15/original_image3044ddc2-b724-4294-b9ab-4e3a245b30
 83.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Cinema Shift Festival is a one-night event that brings togethe
 r films and conversations about how AI is used in filmmaking.\nOn June 5 a
 t the Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema\, you’ll see a curated program of story
 -driven films where AI is part of the creative process - not the focus\, b
 ut the tool. The films are intimate\, funny\, and tense\, showing what thi
 s shift actually looks like on screen.\nAlongside the films\, short conver
 sations explore how creators are working with AI today - from storytelling
  and editing to authorship and rights.\nThis event is for:\n– filmmakers
 \, directors\, and producers exploring new workflows\n– AI creatives and
  technologists working with generative tools\n– VFX artists\, editors\, 
 and production professionals\n– agency creatives\, strategists\, and bra
 nd teams\n– students and emerging creators in film and creative technolo
 gy\nIf you’re curious about where filmmaking is heading - and want to se
 e it\, not just hear about it - this is a rare chance to experience it in 
 a cinema setting.\nGet tickets: https://luma.com/CinemaShiftFestival2026
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/cinema-shift-festival-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
