BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Afrorack\, Phedre\, Arc & Texture
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T235900
UID:blogto-233816@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/17/original_image7201a946-381d-47ab-825e-691eecfc76
 63.jpg
DESCRIPTION:AFRORACK\nBrian Bamanya\, known professionally as Afrorack\, i
 s a Ugandan multidisciplinary artist\, engineer\, and musician who has pio
 neered Africa’s first DIY modular synthesizer. Driven by a passion for e
 lectronics and a desire to make modular synthesis accessible in Uganda\, B
 amanya constructed his own synthesizer using locally sourced components an
 d self-taught engineering skills. This innovative instrument\, also named 
 “The Afrorack\,” serves as both his artistic moniker and a symbol of h
 is commitment to blending technology with African musical traditions. He h
 as appeared at several international festivals which include Sonar\, Rewir
 e\, Elevate\, Dakar Art Biennale and CTM among others.\nIn May 2022\, Afro
 rack released his self-titled debut album\, The Afrorack\, through the Uga
 ndan label Hakuna Kulala. The album showcases his unique approach to elect
 ronic music\, mergingpolyrhythmic structures inherent in African music wit
 h elements of acid\, techno\, and ambientsounds. Tracks like “African Dr
 um Machine” exemplify his use of Euclidean rhythm sequencing to create c
 omplex\, algorithmic patterns that echo traditional East African rhythms. 
 The album was received with popular acclaim making it to several music wri
 ters’ best albums of 2022 including The Wire Magazine top 50 albums of 2
 022\, The Quietus best of 2022 and He has also been featured on the BBC wo
 rld service radio.\nAfrorack’s innovative work continues to inspire a ne
 w generation of musicians and technologists\, bridging the gap between tra
 ditional African music and contemporary electronic soundscapes.\nPHÈDRE\n
 Phèdre is the electronic duo of Daniel Lee and apè Aliermo\, based in Tk
 aronto/Toronto. Emerging from experimental pop\, their sound has evolved i
 nto fast-paced\, bass-driven sets blending sequencers\, samplers and synth
 s into kinetic\, genre-bending performances. Performed entirely on live ha
 rdware\, the duo weaves club\, jungle\, breakbeat and techno influences\, 
 through a blend of playful rhythms and disruption. Phèdre returns with a 
 raw\, semi-improvised live set shaped by their new album Liquid Constancy.
  Expect deep grooves\, sharp turns\, and a pulse that never lets go.\nARC 
 & TEXTURE\nArc & Texture is the sonic unification of Toronto-based sound a
 rtists Vanese Smith (Pursuit Grooves\, Mo:delic Arts) and Caleb Klager (MM
 RI\, wavemap). Blending their respective expertise in unorthodox cinematic
  percussive sounds with emotive modular synthesis tones\, they create laye
 red bass-driven techno\, dub\, and ambient live sets that stirs equal part
 s body and mind. Each set is completely improvised\, unfolding deep\, uniq
 ue auditory encounters between performer and listener. Coming off recent p
 erformances at MUTEK Montréal\, Toronto’s Long Winter\, and a guest-lec
 ture series at Queen’s University\, they continue to deliver thought-pro
 voking and multi-disciplinary experiences.
LOCATION:BSMT 254
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/afrorack-phedre-arc-texture-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
